1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Open the WebMCP command center.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
21 tools: 14 read-only and 6 human-governed.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The authenticated workspace registers page-native tools.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The browser uses the signed-in session, not a separate credential.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
First, list the authorized OrgMemory spaces.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Then request a briefing before raising payments concurrency.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The briefing returns six memories and a requires-approval verdict.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Incident, dependency, decision, procedure, arguments, counts, and latency are visible.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:01,000
The first agent retrieves incident history and the blast radius.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
It answers from structured memory, not scraped UI.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Verified new knowledge enters a proposal.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Nothing is saved until a person approves it.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Session two is a different agent with no shared chat.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:34,000
It starts with the approved organizational memory.

15
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Add Knowledge accepts documents, repositories, Slack, and connected sources.

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
The original source is preserved before extraction.

17
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Memories are atomic, typed, scoped, confidence-ranked, and current.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Incidents, procedures, dependencies, and decisions remain distinct.

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Profiles are assembled from current authorized memories.

20
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Payments combines its decision, procedure, and dependency.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
The graph connects evidence, memories, services, and relationships.

22
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
It preserves provenance, updates, contradictions, ownership, and blast radius.

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Memory Work activates the evidence needed for an outcome.

24
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Connector actions remain behind explicit approval.

25
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The Outcome Loop tracks context served, action taken, and result observed.

26
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,000
This demo's briefing appears as an open ledger row.

27
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Ingest. Extract. Retrieve through WebMCP.

28
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Approve writes, prepare work, and record outcomes.
